<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15874" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ēōs</span></b>  (only in nom.),
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἠώς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the dawn</i> (pure
			Lat. Aurora), <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 3, 877</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 389</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Oet.
			615</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>, <i>the East</i>, <i>the Orient</i>, <i><span class="en">Luc. 9,
			544</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ē^ōus</span></b> , a, um.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			Adj.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>Belonging to the morning</i>, <i>morning-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Atlantides absconduntur,</span>”
				i. e. <i>disappear</i>, <i>set in the morning</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 221</span></i>
			.—More freq., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>Belonging to the east</i>, <i>eastern</i>, <i>orient</i> (a favorite word of the
			Aug. poets): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domus Aurorae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop. 2, 14, 10</span></i>
			 (3, 10, 8 M.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 3, 10: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arabes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tib.
					3, 2, 24</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domus Arabum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 2, 115</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					1, 489</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caelum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					4, 197</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ripa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 5, 21: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tib.
					2, 2, 16</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fluctus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					Epod. 2, 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">partes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					C. 1, 35, 31</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 1, 140</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orbis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 3, 466</span></i>
			; 5, 557 et saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ē^ōus</span></b> , i,
			m.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> Like <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠῷος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστήρ</span>), <i>the morning-star</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 1,
				288</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. 3, 588</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11,
			4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>An inhabitant of the East</i>, <i>an
				Oriental</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. Tr. 4, 9, 22</span></i> Jahn; <i><span class="en">id. Am. 1,
				15, 29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 2, 3, 43
			sq.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>The name of one of the horses of the sun</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2,
				153</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
